\end{align*} for  
\begin{align*}  
n \in \mathbb{N} \backslash \{ 0 \}.  
\end{align*}  
This substitution makes we can start simplifying. We then rewrite  
\begin{align*}  
L &= a_{1} + a_{2} + \cdots + a_{2009} + a_{2010} \\
  &= \log_2 \frac{1}{0} + \log_2 \frac{2}{1} + \cdots + \log_2 \frac{2009}{2008} + \log_2 \frac{2010}{2009} \\
  &= (\log_2 1 - \log_2 0) + (\log_2 2 - \log_2 1) + \cdots + (\log_2 2009 - \log_2 2008) + (\log_2 2010 - \log_2 2009) \\
  &= \log_2 2010 - 0
\end{align*} where we are allowed to use the property  
\begin{align*}  
a - b = \log_2 2^{a - b} = \log_2 \frac{2^{a}}{2^{b}},  
\end{align*}  
and also note that  
\begin{align*}  
0 = \log_2 1 = \log_2 \frac{1}{0}.  
\end{align*}  
Therefore the largest integer less than this is the largest integer less than  
